#
# The fingerprint sensor's swipes.
#
# The Sunwave HAL reports swipes on the sensor -- as keys of the sf-keys input
# device, see rootdir/usr/keylayout/sf-keys.kl -- only with "navigation" on in
# its configuration. The stock /vendor/etc/sw_config.xml leaves it off and
# turns key emulation on instead, which the HAL treats as the alternative: the
# sensor then sends a tap for every touch, swipes included.
#
# The HAL takes the first of /vendor/etc/sw_config.xml and
# /system/etc/sw_config.xml that it can open (sf_config_sync() in
# sunwave.fingerprint.default.so), so a file of our own at the second path is
# not enough while the vendor's exists. It is mounted over the vendor's
# instead, before the HAL starts with class hal on boot. The vendor image stays
# as it is.
on post-fs
    mount none /system/etc/sw_config.xml /vendor/etc/sw_config.xml bind
